# The container's own server, and only that. This is NOT the wheel.cuatro.dev
# site block. TLS, the Cloudflare Origin CA certificate and the response headers
# all live in the shared Caddyfile on the box (/home/deploy/cs-tracker/Caddyfile,
# read by the one Caddy that owns ports 80 and 443 for the whole estate), which
# reverse-proxies the hostname to this container by its compose alias. This file
# is what `caddy:2` inside the image reads: plain HTTP on :80, static files,
# nothing else.
#
# `try_files {path} /index.html` keeps what GitHub Pages did until 2026-09-13,
# where `404.html` was a byte-identical copy of `index.html`: any unknown path
# gets the application. The application has no routes, so this is the whole
# fallback and it stays one line (Story 2-25, AD-20).
#
# The shell (`index.html`, however it was reached) is `no-cache` so a browser
# revalidates it on every visit (the ETag makes that a 304) instead of applying
# heuristic freshness and, weeks after a redeploy, asking for hashed bundles
# the new image no longer has; the hashed assets keep Caddy's default caching.
# `route` fixes the order: Caddy runs `header` before `try_files` otherwise, so
# the matcher would see `/no/such/path` unrewritten and that response would
# ship without the header.
#
# Indentation is tabs, which is what `caddy fmt` produces.

:80 {
	root * /srv
	@shell path / /index.html
	route {
		try_files {path} /index.html
		header @shell Cache-Control "no-cache"
		file_server
	}
}

# For the record: the wheel.cuatro.dev site block as appended to the shared
# Caddyfile on the box by Story 2-25, and mirrored in cuatro-portfolio's
# ops/routing-inventory.md. Nothing reads it from here. It is reproduced so the
# image is self-describing and the record has a source in this repository.
#
# wheel.cuatro.dev {
# 	tls /data/origin-ca/origin.pem /data/origin-ca/origin.key
# 	header {
# 		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
# 		X-Frame-Options "DENY"
# 		Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
# 	}
# 	reverse_proxy list-wheel:80
# }
